<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mongol invasion of Volga Bulgaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1223–1236</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-invasion-of-europe">Mongol invasion of Europe</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mongol invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> was the series of campaigns from 1223 to 1236 against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgar</a> state on the middle Volga. After the Volga Bulgars ambushed a Mongol force returning from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalka">Kalka</a> in 1223, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batu-khan">Batu Khan</a>'s great western campaign destroyed their cities, including the capital Bilär, in 1236, and the region became part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>.</p></div>
